In the VSCode screenshot and the ESLint output you see a crash inside the “constructor-super” rule. You have a simple ES6 class:

  class Extender {}
  class BugProof extends Extender {
    constructor(props) {
      super(props);
      try {
        let arr = [];
        for (let a of arr) {}
      } catch (err) {}
    }
  }

When you save or add a blank line at the end, ESLint trips over a “Cannot read property 'superCalled' of undefined” error and reports a “Parsing error: Unexpected token” at that last blank line. The crash is coming from inside the constructor-super rule’s code-path logic rather than from a true syntax problem in your file.
